cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use pygeofetch in your research, operational workflows, or educational 
  materials, please cite it using the metadata below. Citing the software helps 
  the authors demonstrate research impact, secure future funding, and continue 
  developing open-source geospatial tools for the Global South.

type: software
title: "pygeofetch: A Unified Python Framework for Multi-Provider Satellite Data Acquisition, Pre-download Quality Control, and Geospatial Processing"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EOCoreINT/pygeofetch"
url: "https://appiahkubis14.github.io/pygeofetch-docs/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"

abstract: >
  pygeofetch is a unified, open-source Python library that abstracts satellite 
  Earth observation data access across 22+ providers (including Copernicus, 
  USGS, Planetary Computer, and AWS Earth) through a single, consistent API. 
  Beyond simple data retrieval, pygeofetch introduces a novel "Preflight Gate" 
  that evaluates stack viability pre-download, preventing the acquisition of 
  terabytes of decorrelated or orbit-deficient data by validating Sentinel-1 
  TOPS burst synchronization (<5 ms requirement) and implementing orbit-cascading 
  fallbacks. Furthermore, it features the first pure-Python, Windows-native 
  end-to-end InSAR processing chain, including native SBAS inversion, PS-InSAR 
  hybrid selection, amplitude-based offset tracking, and zero-configuration 
  SNAPHU integration. Designed with reproducibility and accessibility in mind, 
  pygeofetch democratizes advanced geospatial analysis for researchers, 
  government analysts, and students in Africa and the Global South.

